NAME
       x509_parse, x509_verify_chain, x509_check_host - certificates

SYNOPSIS
       #include <x509.h>

       int x509_parse(const uint8_t *der, size_t n, x509_cert_t *out);
       int x509_store_load_pem(const char *path, x509_store_t *store);
       int x509_verify_chain(const x509_cert_t *chain, int n,
                             const x509_store_t *store);
       int x509_check_host(const x509_cert_t *c, const char *host);
       int x509_verify_sig(...);

DESCRIPTION
       Parses DER certificates and verifies a chain against a trust
       store loaded from PEM, checking the signatures, the validity
       dates and the basic constraints.

       x509_check_host matches the host name against the subject
       alternative names, including wildcards, and falls back to the
       common name. A chain that verifies for the wrong host is still
       the wrong certificate, so both checks are needed.

       The trust store shipped with the system is /etc/ssl/certs.

RETURN VALUE
       0 when the check passes, negative otherwise.

SEE ALSO
       tls(3), crypto(3), wget(1)
